  "body": "## What\n\nAdds `JOURNAL.md` to `.gitignore`, next to the existing `WORKING-NOTES.md` entry.\n\n## Why\n\n`WORKING-NOTES.md` (the local operator notes) had grown to 6,250 lines, roughly\na fifth of which was a duplicated changelog. It has been split in two:\n\n- `WORKING-NOTES.md` — the durable half: practices, preferences, methods, lessons, open debt.\n- `JOURNAL.md` — the dated half: per-release arcs, the old version tables, point-in-time machine state.\n\nOnly the first was ignored, so the new file sat untracked and visible. A\n`git add -A` from a fresh worktree would have staged ~126 KB of local notes.\n\nBoth files are operator notes, not repository content — the version history they\nrecord already lives in `git tag` and GitHub releases, which are authoritative\nwhere the journal disagrees.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n$ git check-ignore -v JOURNAL.md WORKING-NOTES.md\n.gitignore:23:JOURNAL.md\tJOURNAL.md\n.gitignore:22:WORKING-NOTES.md\tWORKING-NOTES.md\n\n$ grep -rln gitignore tests/ smoke/\n(no matches — nothing asserts this file's contents)\n```\n\n## Version\n\nNo bump. `.gitignore` is not a production path per CLAUDE.md.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nNone. One line added, one comment reworded; no runtime, packaging or install\nsurface is touched.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
