    "message": "chore: gitignore JOURNAL.md alongside WORKING-NOTES.md\n\nWORKING-NOTES.md has been split in two. The durable half keeps that name; the\ndated half — per-release arcs, old version tables, point-in-time machine state —\nmoved to JOURNAL.md so it stays off the read path. Only WORKING-NOTES.md was\nignored, leaving the new file untracked and visible, where a `git add -A` from a\nfresh worktree would stage ~126 KB of local notes.\n\nBoth are local operator notes, not repository content: the version history they\nrecord is already in git tags and GitHub releases, which are authoritative.\n\nVerification:\n  git check-ignore -v JOURNAL.md  -> .gitignore:23:JOURNAL.md  JOURNAL.md\n  grep -rl gitignore tests/ smoke/ -> no test reads this file\n\nNo version bump: .gitignore is not a production path per CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
